## polars

- Pass `schema_overrides=` (and `columns=`) when reading, and parse dates with `pl.col("taken_at").str.to_datetime(TIMESTAMP_FORMAT)`, keeping `strict=True`, the default, so a malformed value raises.
- Use `pl.Enum([...])` for a label column with a fixed set of values, defined once as a shared constant like any other categorical dtype.
{% endif %}
